{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778265256,"nonce":"bpCdg73NCd/Kr2fDWkFxR0JaFL0=","title":"Compositional hidden-state smoothness loss term (||ḣ_t||²)","message":"Adds `StateDerivativeLoss` to `feedbax.loss` — a generic, compositional time-derivative penalty on a state substate.\n\n## Surface\n- Class: `feedbax.loss.StateDerivativeLoss(label, where, time_axis=1, norm)`\n- Default `where`: `lambda state: state.net.hidden`. Default `norm`: squared L2 over feature axes. Default `time_axis`: 1 (feedbax's `(trial, time, ...)` rollout convention).\n- Returns a per-trial loss density via `mean(||x_t - x_{t-1}||²)` along the time axis. `where` may return either a single `Array` or a `PyTree[Array]`; leaf contributions sum.\n\n## Properties verified by tests\n- Zero on a constant trajectory; closed-form on linear ramps.\n- Correct gradient sign (penalises larger temporal jumps).\n- Wireable into `CompositeLoss`; weight=0 is a no-op (preserves existing configurations).\n- Invariant to leading ensemble-vmap axis and to hidden size (and thus to RNN cell type — GRU, vanilla, leaky).\n\n## Motivation\nSurfaced from rlrmp issue `efc4d68`: trajectory-level replicate variability in delayed-reach controllers needs a smoothness regulariser. Shahbazi, Codol, Michaels \u0026 Gribble 2025 (https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.03.26.645562, Eq. 1) use exactly this term at weight 1e-3.\n\n## Cross-refs\n- rlrmp issue: `efc4d68` (motivation, A/B baseline retrain plan).\n- Branch: `feature/loss-hidden-derivative` off `develop`.","files":null}]}